<block><txt break.before="1">An Act to make provision for extending the
application in the State of laws of other States or Territories relating to
the merger of banks, and for other purposes.</txt></block></tier>
</content>


<content type="body">

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9848c40d-2bbc-4729-bfd8-e057516e085a"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading id="sec.1-he"
guid="_e936a649-24ce-44c9-8774-59f9c14eab65"><b>Name of
Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act is the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
refid="act-1996-064" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Bank Mergers
(Application of Laws) Act 1996</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0806e7c9-20f7-4249-bdd1-486446749e40"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading id="sec.2-he"
guid="_6e9a2fd4-18f1-4457-b42f-62ed857984e3"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act commences on the date of
assent.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1bd45132-11f0-4873-97ec-e6dca16490de"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading id="sec.3-he"
guid="_fef74ac0-f881-435b-96b7-4862dd77cc81"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="def.merger"
guid="_91c49360-8536-4f5a-ae87-c5181e6ba52c"
type="definition"><b><i>merger</i></b></defterm> includes the acquisition of
property and assets, and the assumption of liabilities, of a bank by another
bank or the transfer of property and assets and liabilities of a bank to
another bank.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm id="def.proclaimedlaw"
guid="_94404e09-2c24-4fa8-ab1b-1e7592773c82"
type="definition"><b><i>proclaimed law</i></b></defterm> means a law of
another State or Territory that is declared under this Act to be a law to
which this Act applies.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f4f98644-3470-4e5a-9ac4-b8d3a76e3d76"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading id="sec.4-he"
guid="_71667d96-3add-40f3-ba62-0b5764e4730d"><b>Proclamations</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_38b0debe-ba6b-4675-a069-29e79e8a7cda"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may by proclamation declare a law of
another State or Territory providing for or relating to the merger of banks to
be a law to which this Act applies.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e4b14028-66d3-45a9-bf06-33839de818c0"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Such a proclamation may:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.a" guid="_9f7c8ee9-45fe-4305-b614-d6bbe40a4e26"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">exclude specified provisions of the proclaimed
law from the operation of this Act, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.b" guid="_cd19611e-527a-4d1d-9703-67358dc1e64b"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">modify the effect of specified provisions of the
proclaimed law in their application under this Act, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.c" guid="_fc9a5fbc-cb41-404b-9672-4211bd3fabd7"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">without limiting paragraph (b), supplement the
provisions of the proclaimed law in their application under this Act with
additional provisions that apply by virtue of this Act,
and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.d" guid="_b5fbb6f9-f0c5-429e-abc1-0100ea829e7c"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">provide that a requirement has been made under
section 6.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_76689e70-6403-4be7-a7d0-f51edfd1c303"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A proclamation under this Act may be amended or
repealed by a further proclamation.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.4"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ba9f66f6-12b6-4950-a5cb-3da3cc16d417"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A proclamation may be made in respect of a law of
another State or Territory whether or not that law has commenced in that State
or Territory.</txt></block></tier>

<note id="sec.4-note" guid="_eef76e86-e167-409f-8274-507914e5cc67"
type="editorial"><heading id="sec.4-note-he"
guid="_ebfb164d-e627-4ba9-92c1-bffd12aa12e4"><b>Editorial
note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">For proclamations under this section, see
Gazettes No 110 of 27.9.1996; No 137 of 29.11.1996 and No 46 of 1.5.1997, p
2423.</txt></block></note>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0ce6a05c-b904-493c-9f92-0b53d83e3140"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading id="sec.5-he"
guid="_c26a8668-848c-4d5d-b414-0440584a398a"><b>Extension of proclaimed
law</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e4ecdcb8-9a1f-46fc-9306-aa8d7a9a9cb0"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The application of a proclaimed law is extended
so that it applies in this State as if it were a law of this
State.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_15cc54f2-c88c-4e12-8983-d39bee17daac"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">However, in its application in this State a
proclaimed law is to be read subject to:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.5-ssec.2-para1.a" guid="_244f93f9-d38b-41d7-aa8a-8df3093795a6"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the exclusions, modifications and
supplementations set out in the relevant proclamation, as amended by any
further proclamations, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.5-ssec.2-para1.b" guid="_205cbef2-7251-4018-988e-0b7678778b5f"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the provisions of subsection
(4).</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6d03b57a-5f00-4a99-aff7-703843d3c8b4"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The application in this State of a proclaimed law
is not affected by its amendment or repeal in the State or Territory in which
it was enacted, except to the extent provided by the relevant proclamation, as
amended by any further proclamations.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.4"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_42e2f772-af69-4397-9816-febd918253a3"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Provisions of a proclaimed law relating
to:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.5-ssec.4-para1.a" guid="_49849961-63f0-402d-b746-82e6baf7ccbf"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the provision of government guarantees,
or</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.5-ssec.4-para1.b" guid="_d7af52f7-81e3-4e92-9629-b50e68d38453"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">exemption from payment of duties, taxes, charges,
rates or other imposts,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">are excluded from the operation of subsection (1),
except to the extent that the relevant proclamation, as amended by any further
proclamations, includes them (and subject to any modifications or
supplementations specified in the proclamation).</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fbaaa33a-b565-43cd-8855-5f5925bd94ee"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading id="sec.6-he"
guid="_a6c4e998-e9c8-4ce0-bfbf-d16e585338f2"><b>Payment of amount instead of
State duties or other imposts</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c6aacfe6-7228-4173-98b0-c83cf0b3f145"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Despite any other provision of this Act, the
application in this State of a proclaimed law does not take effect until any
requirement made under this section, and referred to in the proclamation under
this Act, has been complied with and the Treasurer has given a certificate
under subsection (4) to that effect.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d97d1412-47c3-49d4-8dc4-81c29ad28579"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Treasurer may require one or more of the
banks concerned:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.a" guid="_a522b6d8-086f-4f2f-8286-4b37bcc503ad"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to pay to the Treasurer instead of all duties,
taxes, charges, rates or other imposts for which the bank or banks concerned
would be liable under the law of this State as a result of, or in connection
with, the merger an amount that is, in the opinion of the Treasurer, proper in
the circumstances, and</txt></block></li>
<li id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.b" guid="_e3f4dbbc-f613-4e6e-bce0-558db4a37adf"
provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to pay that amount before the commencement of the
proclamation or to give a written undertaking to pay the amount on or after
that commencement.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a3186aac-b942-4c63-9558-0131dbe9a2ff"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The amount payable to the Treasurer is to be
determined by the Treasurer in accordance with such principles as the
Treasurer thinks appropriate.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.4"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c964bbca-0ab0-4b67-b6ab-c9da5ff9acf0"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Treasurer must, when satisfied that a
requirement under this section has been complied with, give the bank subject
to the requirement a certificate stating that the requirement has been
complied with.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.5"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_aadfb815-b305-495c-9d68-28f5f9e5670a"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(5)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Treasurer must, when satisfied that an amount
required under this section to be paid on or after the commencement of a
proclamation has been paid, give the bank subject to the requirement a
certificate stating that the amount has been paid.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.6"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f44e87c2-cd9e-414c-bb8d-e6867f34742e"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(6)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If a certificate is given under this section
stating that a requirement to pay an amount has been complied with or that an
amount has been paid, the bank given the certificate is not liable for any
further duties, taxes, charges, rates or other imposts of the kind referred to
in subsection (2).</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.7"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9f4e2aaa-f413-471b-a1e1-07d38dcec723"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(7)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A certificate under this section is, for all
purposes and in all courts, tribunals and proceedings, conclusive evidence of
the matters certified.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.8"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4d620217-f97c-4d95-97c1-9e829e40cfba"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(8)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section does not apply to any fee or charge
payable to the Registrar-General in respect of any act, dealing or other
transaction relating to land.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_755da811-163c-4103-a791-a340b151ec00"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading id="sec.7-he"
guid="_a9c5c742-7fb1-4a8f-9d0f-2a2c50306fa9"><b>Review of
Act</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_12c9b6ed-17c0-4823-985f-a3932e05f731"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister is to review this Act to determine
whether the policy objectives of the Act remain valid and whether the terms of
the Act remain appropriate for securing those
objectives.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_27009b3c-e7ab-453a-a9cd-e2bbc2fb91fd"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The review is to be undertaken as soon as
possible after the period of 5 years from the date of assent to this
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.3"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_37751a11-ac07-48a5-b2fc-b3fede335700"></attrib>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A report on the outcome of the review is to be
tabled in each House of Parliament within 12 months after the end of the
